# `scripts/lib/write-publication-files.ts` writes a LICENSE and a README.md beside each package.json before
# packing, because npm packs both whether or not `files` names them. Both are derived - the licence from
# the root file, the page from fields the manifest already declares - so neither is committed.
#
# Declared here rather than at the repository root, and that is the whole point of this file. The root
# `.gitignore` is SEED: `packages/assets/build.ts` copies it verbatim into the body every consumer
# receives from `ploaness init`. `packages/ploaness/biome.json` there is inert in a Payload project - no
# such path exists - but `packages/*/LICENSE` is NOT inert, because a Payload workspace with `packages/*`
# members has real licence files in exactly those places, and the seed would have told git to ignore them.
*/LICENSE
*/README.md
